I'm not saying either, though. I think those gismu which lack the places of
their compatriots /do/ need them, and not merely because their lack makes
them irregular. For example, if you wanted to say that ko'a is the adopted
sister of ko'e, you could easily do so, as mensi is "x1 is the sister of x2
by bond/tie x3". However, if you wanted to say that ko'a is the adopted
daughter of ko'i, you have a more difficult time, because tixnu lacks the
by bond x3: "x1 is the daughter of parent(s) x2 (no necessarily
biological)".

